.TH TERMTV 1 "2026-08-07" "termtv" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
termtv \- hardware-aware terminal video renderer
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B termtv
[\fICOMMAND\fR] [\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
termtv renders video in a terminal using ANSI half-block characters.
It supports a native \fB.ttv1\fR format and can stream source video or
camera capture through FFmpeg.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B convert \fIinput\fR \fIoutput.ttv\fR
Convert any FFmpeg-readable input to the native \fB.ttv1\fR format.
.TP
.B play \fIfile.ttv\fR
Play a native \fB.ttv1\fR file.
.TP
.B play-source \fIinput\fR
Stream any FFmpeg-readable source directly to the terminal.
.TP
.B playlist list|play \fIfile.m3u\fR
List or play entries from an M3U playlist.
.TP
.B camera on|off|list
Stream, stop, or list V4L2 camera devices.
.TP
.B accel-info
List available hardware acceleration backends.
.TP
.B help
Show usage information.
.TP
.B completions \fIbash|zsh|fish\fR
Print a shell completion script for the requested shell.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-\-width " " \fIN\fR
Output width in terminal cells.
.TP
.BR \-\-height " " \fIN\fR
Output height in terminal cells.
.TP
.BR \-\-fps " " \fIN\fR
Target frames per second.
.TP
.BR \-\-hwaccel " " \fIID\fR
Hardware backend: auto, vaapi, qsv, cuda, vdpau, drm, opencl, vulkan.
.TP
.BR \-\-ambience " " \fIID\fR
Ambience mode: off, pulse, strobe.
.TP
.BR \-\-color
Force ANSI color output.
.TP
.BR \-\-no-color
Disable ANSI color output.
.TP
.BR \-\-device " " \fIPATH\fR
V4L2 device path (camera only).
.TP
.BR \-\-capture-width " " \fIN\fR
Camera capture width.
.TP
.BR \-\-capture-height " " \fIN\fR
Camera capture height.
.TP
.BR \-\-behavior " " \fIlive|photo\fR
Camera behavior.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ./.termtv.toml
Local configuration file.
.TP
.I ~/.config/termtv/config.toml
User configuration file.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ffmpeg (1)
